        answer: "Usually yes — accept the first offer you receive. A job offer in hand reduces anxiety for subsequent interview attempts (you're trying to upgrade, not trying to survive), and IT services joining timelines are often 12-18 months post-graduation giving you time to continue preparing. The only situation where declining makes sense: if you have a strong product company process in progress within the same placement season AND you're willing to risk being unplaced. This is a high-risk decision — consult your placement officer about your specific college's rules (some colleges require you to stop interviewing after accepting any offer)."
